      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Try to prepare yourself on API development, either Django or NodeJS/ExpressJS. Also practice SQL queries from SQL 50, and learn the basics of designing schemas.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "For the resume, follow the format of Jake’s resume, and try to keep it 1 page. Properly include your experience, projects and skills, and make sure you can speak about anything that you put in your resume.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure you have a proper introduction ready, which briefly covers your education, your internship experience and high impact projects. Also, create an introduction which aligns with the company’s principles.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 2
        },
        {
          "text": "If you switch languages for DSA, be clear about your reason, it's not about which language is 'better', but what helps you learn and think better.",
          "category": "Coding preparation",
          "page": 3
        },
        {
          "text": "Make sure that you keep properly explaining the interviewer your thought process behind each and every step, and also make sure to ask doubts on things that might not be clear in the problem statement.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "Explain the cardinality of each relationship you are creating (one-one, one-many, many-many).",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 4
        },
        {
          "text": "I would advise learning CTEs while solving SQL 50, because they are a powerful way of dividing your SQL query into manageable and easy-to-understand sequential steps.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Don’t prepare scripted answers. Reflect on your journey, speak from the heart, and be honest. This round isn’t about checking boxes, it’s about understanding who you are and what drives you.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Have a good idea about the companies that you have interned at. The interviewer might ask certain questions like when was the company founded, or how old was your mentor in the company, not to grill you, but to verify authenticity and see how well you know your own experiences.",
          "category": "HR preparation",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Craft a solid self-introduction — it's your first impression, so make it count.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Take notes during the pre-placement talk — they can help you frame personalized questions during the interviews.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Practice a backend framework like Django or Express — learn to set up a server, design schemas, and build basic APIs beforehand.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Focus on mastering fundamentals and recognizing patterns, not chasing streaks or ratings.",
          "category": "Coding preparation",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Use Indiabix and GFG to revise fundamentals of DBMS, OS, OOPs and CCN. DBMS is the main priority, as the interviews revolved around being able to apply the concepts you learned in DBMS.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "LeetCode’s Top 50 SQL Questions are more than enough to get a strong grip on SQL basics and variations.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Don’t panic in interviews — it's okay to ask for help; interviewers are usually very supportive. Think aloud throughout each interview — it helps the interviewer follow your approach and gives them a chance to guide you if needed.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 6
        }
